# PREFLIGHT_2026-08-27_k_lens.md). Reuses library_lens.js's own scoring
# discipline against the library-at-large rather than retired-build lineage.
# Tracked so the instrument travels with the corpus it scans.
!/tools/k_lens.js
# The boot hook, 2026-08-17 (Kevin's mark: "set up the hook layer"). It reads
# LEARNED.md and injects it at SessionStart, which is what makes the route a
# filesystem fact rather than an instruction. Tracked so it travels with the
# deposit it carries. The settings.json that calls it stays out by the rule
# above, so a clone gets the script and wires it by hand.
!/tools/boot_hook.py
# The harness boot layer, 2026-08-31 (Kevin's mark: "add them to the
# allowlist"). Same gap boot_hook.py's own entry above already named,
# never closed for its sibling: boot_hook_harness.py is wired into
# settings.json's SessionStart hook exactly the way boot_hook.py is, and
# calls the three instruments below with --summary on every boot, but none
# of the five files were tracked — a boot path that does not survive a
# checkout is not routed, and this one wasn't. Closed the same day
# agent_usage_check.js was built (skill/agent usage had no instrument for
# agents at all before this).
!/tools/boot_hook_harness.py
!/tools/check_harness.js
!/tools/framing_check_skills.js
!/tools/lens_usage_check.js
!/tools/agent_usage_check.js
# Real-invocation siblings, same day, same mark: the mark-log signal above
# undercounted (full-development: 1 mark-log mention, 38 real invocations)
# and overcounted (record-audit: 3 mentions, 0 real invocations) — Kevin's
# own catch. These read session transcripts directly instead.
!/tools/skill_invocation_check.js
!/tools/agent_invocation_check.js
# The deposit pipeline itself, 2026-08-30/31. Same gap as the harness files
# above, caught later: build_deposit.js / build_deposit_public.js /
# deposit_lib.js are the actual mechanism that ships this corpus to
# Bluescontact/NESI, run by hand each time, and were never tracked.
# typology_classify.js added 2026-08-31 (Kevin's mark: "proceed on 1" —
# THE TYPOLOGY, ported from nesi/conductor/tension_table.py).
!/tools/build_deposit.js
!/tools/build_deposit_public.js
!/tools/deposit_lib.js
!/tools/typology_classify.js
# The arrangement organ, 2026-08-31 (Kevin's mark: "we need an organ on
# each side of the pipeline... The organ we are running now is on the
# other end.. prefiltering."). build_deposit_public.js is the source-side
# organ: decides WHAT qualifies. This is the destination-side organ: reads
# the already-filtered deposit and composes it into one navigable index —
# nesi_deposit_public/index.html — instead of leaving a visitor to
# cross-reference raw folders and JSON by hand.
!/tools/build_deposit_index.js
